bounds + u-range truncation bounds + spatial Riemann enclosure via
exact-kernel derivative moduli). Strongest, heaviest.
(iii) condition-then-CS (RECOMMENDED):
  E[|det H| 1{det<0} 1{f in W} | g=0]
    = integral over W of phi_{mu_t, v_t}(u) * E[|det H| 1{det<0} | f=u] du
    <= Pw_exact * sup_{u in [b-ell, b]} ( sqrt(E[det^2 H | g=0, f=u])
         * min(1, sqrt(P(det<0 | g=0, f=u))) ).
H | (g=0, f=u) is Gaussian with mean nu + (cvec/v_t)*(u - mu_t) and
covariance Sigma - cvec cvec^T / v_t; E[det^2 | f=u] is an explicit quartic
in u via the same Wick machinery; its sup over the width-ell window is
certified by endpoint evaluation plus a derivative pad. Linear in Pw ->
preserves the O(r^3) channel class. Expected (measured-grade expectation,
to be certified) to land within O(1) of the current decertified figures at
